            <ArticleTitle>Safe use of glutaraldehyde.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-51; quiz 53-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Glutaraldehyde is an effective chemical for killing micro-organisms that is used in a variety of healthcare settings to rapidly clean instruments. It is highly toxic in even small concentrations and needs to stored and handled carefully. Diane Romano-Woodward explains how nurses can ensure that adequate precautions are taken to prevent harm to staff and patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
